 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Isosurface Filter
-Constructs an isosurface using a critical value (threshold). By default, it renders the isosurface as an empty shell [S2]. To fill the isosurface with a solid color, one must either set an interior solid color/volume (useful for semi-transparent isosurfaces) or apply a fog filter targeting the isosurface [S2].
+Constructs an isosurface using a critical value (threshold) [S2]. By default, it renders the isosurface as an empty shell [S2]. To fill the isosurface with a solid color, one must either set an interior solid color or volume (useful for semi-transparent isosurfaces) or apply a fog filter targeting the isosurface [S2].
+
+### Automatic Isosurface Thresholding
+Computes a default isovalue from the volume data when the user provides special floating-point values (NaN, -inf, +inf) [S3, unofficial]. If `requested_level` is NaN, the system calls `setThreshold(img, nvox, 2)`. If `requested_level` is -inf, it calls `setThreshold(img, nvox, 1)`. If `requested_level` is +inf, it calls `setThreshold(img, nvox, 3)`. Otherwise, the provided value is used directly [S3, unofficial]. The `setThreshold` mode parameter accepts 1 for negative infinity, 2 for NaN, and 3 for positive infinity [S3, unofficial].
 
